  "summary": "Resolves Include-What-You-Use (IWYU) warnings across fuzz tests, fuzz utilities in `src/test/fuzz`, and several internal headers and modules in `src/`. Configures CI to treat IWYU warnings in these files as errors, reformatting the CI list of enforced files to one file per line. Also adds a mapping for standard C library cookie I/O symbols in the IWYU mappings file.",
  "problem": "Fuzz targets and several core headers rely on transitive includes and contain unused headers. Without explicit includes, CI cannot enforce IWYU compliance on the fuzz suite to prevent future header bloat and unintended dependencies.",
